{"subjectId":"operating-systems","id":"concurrency_coding","title":"Concurrency Coding","group":"Concurrency & Locks","order":6,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">Production-grade thread-safe data structures and coordination implementations.</p>\n<section class=\"block\">\n<h3><i class=\"ti ti-terminal\"></i>1. Print Odd and Even (Two Threads)</h3>\n<div class=\"card\">\n<p>Classic interview question coordinating alternating execution using condition variables:</p>\n<figure class=\"code\"><pre><code>#include &lt;iostream&gt;\n#include &lt;thread&gt;\n#include &lt;mutex&gt;\n#include &lt;condition_variable&gt;\n\nstd::mutex mtx;\nstd::condition_variable cv;\nint count = 1;\nconst int MAX_COUNT = 10;\n\nvoid printOdd() {\n    while (count &lt; MAX_COUNT) {\n        std::unique_lock&lt;std::mutex&gt; lock(mtx);\n        cv.wait(lock, []() { return count % 2 != 0; });\n        std::cout &lt;&lt; \"Odd Thread: \" &lt;&lt; count &lt;&lt; std::endl;\n        count++;\n        cv.notify_all();\n    }\n}\n\nvoid printEven() {\n    while (count &lt;= MAX_COUNT) {\n        std::unique_lock&lt;std::mutex&gt; lock(mtx);\n        cv.wait(lock, []() { return count % 2 == 0; });\n        std::cout &lt;&lt; \"Even Thread: \" &lt;&lt; count &lt;&lt; std::endl;\n        count++;\n        cv.notify_all();\n    }\n}</code></pre></figure>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"block\">\n<h3><i class=\"ti ti-box\"></i>2. Bounded Blocking Queue</h3>\n<div class=\"card\">\n<p>Thread-safe blocking queue using a circular array, a mutex, and two condition variables:</p>\n<figure class=\"code\"><pre><code>#include &lt;vector&gt;\n#include &lt;mutex&gt;\n#include &lt;condition_variable&gt;\n\nclass BoundedBlockingQueue {\nprivate:\n    std::vector&lt;int&gt; queue;\n    int capacity;\n    int head = 0;\n    int tail = 0;\n    int size = 0;\n    std::mutex mtx;\n    std::condition_variable not_full;\n    std::condition_variable not_empty;\n\npublic:\n    BoundedBlockingQueue(int cap) : capacity(cap), queue(cap) {}\n\n    void enqueue(int element) {\n        std::unique_lock&lt;std::mutex&gt; lock(mtx);\n        not_full.wait(lock, [this]() { return size &lt; capacity; });\n        \n        queue[tail] = element;\n        tail = (tail + 1) % capacity;\n        size++;\n        \n        not_empty.notify_one();\n    }\n\n    int dequeue() {\n        std::unique_lock&lt;std::mutex&gt; lock(mtx);\n        not_empty.wait(lock, [this]() { return size &gt; 0; });\n        \n        int val = queue[head];\n        head = (head + 1) % capacity;\n        size--;\n        \n        not_full.notify_one();\n        return val;\n    }\n};</code></pre></figure>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"block\">\n<h3><i class=\"ti ti-shield-check\"></i>3. Thread-Safe Counter (Atomic &amp; CAS)</h3>\n<div class=\"card\">\n<p>Implementing a lock-free thread-safe counter using standard hardware Compare-And-Swap (CAS):</p>\n<figure class=\"code\"><pre><code>#include &lt;atomic&gt;\n\nclass LockFreeCounter {\nprivate:\n    std::atomic&lt;int&gt; value{0};\n\npublic:\n    void increment() {\n        int current = value.load();\n        // Optimistic spin loop using Compare-And-Swap (CAS)\n        while (!value.compare_exchange_weak(current, current + 1)) {\n            // If another thread updated value, CAS fails, 'current' is updated, retry.\n        }\n    }\n\n    int getValue() const {\n        return value.load();\n    }\n};</code></pre></figure>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"block\">\n<h3><i class=\"ti ti-lock\"></i>4. Read-Write Lock Implementation</h3>\n<div class=\"card\">\n<p>Implementing a custom Readers-Writer Lock with priority prevention using mutexes and condition variables:</p>\n<figure class=\"code\"><pre><code>#include &lt;mutex&gt;\n#include &lt;condition_variable&gt;\n\nclass RWLock {\nprivate:\n    std::mutex mtx;\n    std::condition_variable cv;\n    int readers = 0;\n    bool writer_active = false;\n    int waiting_writers = 0; // Prevent reader starvation\n\npublic:\n    void lockRead() {\n        std::unique_lock&lt;std::mutex&gt; lock(mtx);\n        cv.wait(lock, [this]() { return !writer_active &amp;&amp; waiting_writers == 0; });\n        readers++;\n    }\n\n    void unlockRead() {\n        std::unique_lock&lt;std::mutex&gt; lock(mtx);\n        readers--;\n        if (readers == 0) {\n            cv.notify_all();\n        }\n    }\n\n    void lockWrite() {\n        std::unique_lock&lt;std::mutex&gt; lock(mtx);\n        waiting_writers++;\n        cv.wait(lock, [this]() { return !writer_active &amp;&amp; readers == 0; });\n        waiting_writers--;\n        writer_active = true;\n    }\n\n    void unlockWrite() {\n        std::unique_lock&lt;std::mutex&gt; lock(mtx);\n        writer_active = false;\n        cv.notify_all();\n    }\n};</code></pre></figure>\n</div>\n</section>"}